{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Application SSO from an Unknown Client Device",
	"Description": "A successful SSO into an application where Okta could not identify the client device. Device-based sign-on policy rules cannot evaluate a device they cannot identify, so an unknown client is how a request slips past a rule that would otherwise have stopped it.\n\nEvent type: user.authentication.sso with client.device unknown or absent\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_successful_application_sso_from_unknown_client_device/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_successful_application_sso_from_unknown_client_device.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "c5e2933b-92f7-5f67-a6e7-4c18cd0f3c00",
	"SearchReference": "75c18ec5-3941-5777-ad84-b7a6aa94ce46"
}